From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:04:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/78] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b: add an EL2
 variant

The Dragon Q8B firmware decides between EL1 and EL2 from the device tree
it is handed: with /chosen/radxa,enable-kvm present and the
"Hypervisor Override" setup option at its default (Auto), it starts the
operating system at EL2 and applies the EL2 changes to the tree itself.

At EL2 the DSPs cannot be started through the PAS interface. From BIOS
260916 on, the firmware starts them itself when it boots an OS at EL2
("Remoteproc firmware preload", default Auto): it keeps the ADSP its
charger driver started and starts the CDSP at ExitBootServices(). Linux
attaches to both.

Iris cannot load its firmware through PAS at EL2 either (the call fails
with -EINVAL). The overlay gives it a "video-firmware" node with the
firmware's own IOMMU stream, so the driver loads and starts the firmware
itself.

The SoC timer node lists only the four EL1 timer interrupts. At EL2 the
kernel runs with VHE and wants the EL2 virtual timer as well, and warns
"VHE-capable CPU without EL2 virtual timer interrupt" without it. Add
the architected PPI 12.

Build the result as sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b-el2.dtb next to the
regular board DTB, the same way as the ThinkPad X13s EL2 variant.
